ers\nEconomic Vitality Incentive Program\nEmployment\nForms & Worksheets\nRequest for Bids/Proposals\nZoning\nTownships\nBurdell Township\nCedar Township\nEvart Township\nHartwick Township\nHersey Township\nHighland Township\nLeRoy Township\nLincoln Township\nMarion Township\nMiddle Branch Township\nOrient Township\nOsceola Township\nRichmond Township\nRose Lake Township\nSherman Township\nSylvan Township\nVisitors\nChambers of Commerce\nCounty Profile\nCounty Parks\nPhoto Gallery\nShare this page\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://migration.revize.com/revize/HTML_Review/osceolami/freeform-fullwidth.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nPrev Next\nSub Menu\nRelated Pages\nCounty Department Directory\nAnnouncements\nBoard / Committee Agendas & Minutes\nGolf Cart / ATV / UTV / ORV Policy\nMap - Crittenden Park\nMap - Rose Lake Park\nParks Rates & Rules Flyer\nParks Rules and Regulations\nParks Survey\nStorage Rates for Boats on Trailers\nParks\nOsceola County Parks\n22054 Professional Drive, Suite A\nReed City, MI 49677\n(231) 832-6130\noscparks@osceolacountymi.gov\nHome Government County Departments Parks\nParks\nParks Director, Vacant\nInterim Director, Tim Ladd - oscadmin@osceolacountymi.gov\n22054 Professional Drive, Suite A\nReed City, MI 49677\n(231) 832-6130\nparksdirector@osceolacountymi.gov\noscparks@osceolacountymi.gov\nCamping Reservation Process\nOur online booking software is live and taking reservations.\nThe 2026 camping season begins on May 1, 2026 and ends on September 26, 2026.\nReservations will be taken up to 6 months in advance. Download the Campspot App!\nClick below for Rose Lake Park reservations for the 2026 season:\nwww.campspot.com/book/rose-lake-park\nClick below for Crittenden Park reservations for the 2026 season:\nwww.campspot.com/book/crittenden-park\nYou may contact the office at (231) 832-6130 for information. After April 11, 2025 please call Rose Lake Park at (231) 534-3907 or Crittenden Park at (231) 349-4654 for reservations.\nRose Lake, Rose Lake Park, Osceola County, Michigan\nThe Osceola County Parks Commission has two separate and unique parks in its park system. They are both situated on a lake, bordered by forest, and offer limitless opportunities for both the sportsman and recreational enthusiast.\nRose Lake Park, located on Rose Lake, and Crittenden Park, located on Big Lake both offer great fishing. Other recreational opportunities include camping, swimming, and other day use activities such as picnic tables, playground, pavilions, etc. Additionally, Rose Lake Park is located near the White Pine Trail and Crittenden Park is located near the Pere Marquette State Trail .\nCamping is available by the day, week, month, or season. You can use the menu bar on the left to view announcements, a map of each park, and other information.\nCome and enjoy clean, well-maintained facilities and grounds, friendly and helpful staff, great swimming and fishing, and a variety of recreational activities.\nRECREATION PLAN AVAILABLE FOR REVIEW\nClick here to review the 2021-2025 Osceola County Recreation Plan\nThe Recreation Plan is non-directive in nature; however, it fulfills several very important objectives:\nIt helps ensure coordination between the Parks Commission and local units of government and governmental entities.\nIt gives the Parks Commission an opportunity to receive formal feedback from the public.\nIt provides the Parks Commission an opportunity to reflect and focus on the direction of their efforts.\nIt supports Goal #11, Action #2 of the Osceola County, Michigan Future Land Use Plan; \"The County Planning Commission and the County Board of Commissioners will maintain an up-to-date countywide recreation plan and apply for appropriate grants to improve recreation opportunities in Osceola County.\"\nIt allows the Parks Commission to apply for grants through the Michigan Natural Resources Trust Fund. In order to do so, the Plan must be filed with, and approved by, the Michigan Department of Natural Resources.\n|\nCrittenden Park\nLocated on Big Lake\n3641 S. 50th Ave.\nSears, MI 49679\n(231) 349-4654\nBoat Launch Nearby\nRose Lake Park\nLocated on Rose Lake\n17726 Youth Dr.\nLeRoy, MI 49655\n(231) 534-3907\nBoat Launch on Site |\n|\n|\nAgendas / Minutes\n2026 Approved Budget for Osceola County\nEmployment\nFOIA Process\nForms & Worksheets\nRequest for Bids / Proposals\nVolunteer Opportunities\nCounty Departments\nYour Opinion Matters\nOsceola County Survey\nVolunteer for a Board or Commission\nOsceola County is an Equal Opportunity Employer\nUSDA Nondiscrimination Statement\nEmployee Resources\nDiscover Osceola County\nsearch\nOsceola County Main Courthouse\n301 W. Upton Avenue\nReed City, MI 49677\nPhone: Refer to Department Directory\n© 2020 Osceola County, MI. All rights reserved.\nPowered by , The Government Website Experts | Login\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nundefined\nundefined\nundefined",
